摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness coding-subscription OAuth: SuperGrok / Grok Build, ChatGPT Plus Codex, Kimi Code, Claude Code. No API-key pasting.","id":"gh:1335737224","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-coding-subscription-oauth","slug":"lninghaha/dsh-coding-subscription-oauth","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","grok-build","oauth"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness coding-subscription OAuth: SuperGrok / Grok Build, ChatGPT Plus Codex, Kimi Code, C"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"laude Code. No API-key pasting."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# 🔐 dsh-coding-subscription-oauth"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**v0.8.7** · formerly `dsh-grok-build`"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Coding-subscription OAuth for DeepSeek Harness.** Use SuperGrok / X Premium (Grok Build), ChatGPT "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"Plus/Pro (Codex), Kimi Code, Claude Pro/Max and Google Antigravity inside DSH — without a second API"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"-key bill and **without pasting any token into chat.**"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"*English · 中文版 · 日本語 · 한국어 · Português (BR) · Español · Français · Deutsch · Русский*"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"> **Upgrade / 升级：** Follow the versioned steps in `INSTALL.md`. `0.8.0` adds opt-in OpenCode Go comp"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"atibility (sticky `x-opencode-session` on the local gateway). Current main pins the shared dispatche"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"r runtime on `dsh-coding-oauth-core@0.1.2` and `undici@7.29.0`, and restricts gateway key reveal/rot"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"ate to loopback access; no configuration, credential, data, or route migration is required. Grok Ima"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"gine retains its explicit pinned dispatcher. Releases from `0.6.2` onward include the strict Cordis "},{"id":"p6s6","text":"injection startup fix and DSH `0.1.1-rc.2` support; keep profile/config/credential files and restart"},{"id":"p6s7","text":" one existing DSH Web process only after updating."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Name change"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Published first as **`dsh-grok-build`** when it only covered Grok Build. The current name matches th"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"e full coding-subscription OAuth surface."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| | Use this | Still works |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| npm (recommended) | Current release is `0.8.7`: `dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-coding-subscript"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ion-oauth@0.8.7` | No legacy npm package was published |\n| GitHub / development | `dsh-coding-subscr"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"iption-oauth` | Previous GitHub repo `dsh-grok-build` was removed |\n| CLI | `dsh-coding-oauth` | `ds"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"h-grok-build` |\n| Cordis plugin id | `llm-grok-build-oauth` | unchanged |\n| Settings HTTP API | `/pl"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"ugins/dsh-grok-build/*` | unchanged |\n| Credential files | `$DSH_HOME/.grok-build-auth.json` and the"},{"id":"p10s6","text":" other `*-oauth-auth.json` files | unchanged |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## ✨ Features"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- 🧽 **Bring your own subscription** — SuperGrok, ChatGPT Plus/Pro, Kimi Code, Claude Pro/Max; no ext"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"ra pay-as-you-go key.\n- 🔑 **Local OAuth, no key-pasting** — authorize in Settings or CLI; access/ref"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"resh tokens never enter chat, logs or HTTP status.\n- 🧩 **One plugin, five providers** — Grok Build ("},{"id":"p12s4","text":"`cli-chat-proxy.grok.com`), Codex, Kimi Code, Claude Code and Google Antigravity.\n- 🛡️ **Secure by d"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"esign** — credential files are owner-only `0600`, atomically written, cross-process locked.\n- ⚙️ **D"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"ynamic catalog** — the selector lists only signed-in routes, labelled `(OAuth)`, including grok-4.6 "},{"id":"p12s7","text":"`xhigh`.\n- 🌐 **Proxy-aware** — proxies only reviewed subscription domains; Kimi China stays direct b"},{"id":"p12s8","text":"y default.\n- 📥 **Manual CLI Pull** — Settings discovers allowlisted official Grok/Codex/Kimi/Claude "},{"id":"p12s9","text":"CLI OAuth files read-only; you pull a one-way copy after preview and overwrite confirmation.\n- 🗂️ **"},{"id":"p12s10","text":"Tabbed Settings** — Accounts, Gateway, Capabilities, and About; remote hosts prefer device-code sign"},{"id":"p12s11","text":"-in with quieter CLI-missing tips; signed-in cards stay collapsed until expanded.\n- 🎛️ **Optional ca"},{"id":"p12s12","text":"pabilities, default off** — Codex search, usage/quota, image generate/edit, Fast, and Grok Imagine a"},{"id":"p12s13","text":"pply live when you turn them on. An additional default-off switch lets non-Codex model routes call C"},{"id":"p12s14","text":"odex image tools while preserving Codex sign-in, session, and attachment-ownership checks.\n- 🔌 **Opt"},{"id":"p12s15","text":"-in local API gateway** — default-off loopback OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible server for your own tools"},{"id":"p12s16","text":", with copyable base URLs and Bearer key; never a public relay.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Problems this plugin solves"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"These are the searches and DSH errors that usually lead here. If one of them is your tab title, you "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"are in the right repo."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| You searched / saw | What was actually broken | What this plugin does |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| SuperGrok / X Premium in DSH, “Grok Build vs `api.x.ai`” | The built-in `xai` route is the **pay-a"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"s-you-go API**. Coding-plan inference is `cli-chat-proxy.grok.com` | Dedicated `grok-build` route + "},{"id":"p16s3","text":"official CLI fingerprint headers (`X-XAI-Token-Auth`, `x-grok-client-identifier`, `x-grok-client-ver"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"sion`) so you do not get a silent 403 |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Supported providers"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| Provider | Route | Auth | Coexists with |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| **xAI Grok Build** | `grok-build` | SuperGrok / X Premium OAuth | `xai` |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Optional capabilities"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"All eight switches start **off** and apply **live** (no restart): `codexSearch`, `codexImages`, `cod"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"exImageEdits`, `codexImagesAnyModel`, `codexUsage`, `codexFast`, `grokImagineImage`, and `grokImagin"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"eVideo`. `codexImagesAnyModel` only relaxes the calling-model route gate; it still requires signed-i"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"n Codex, `codexImages` (and the edits flag for edit), and keeps session attachment ownership and edi"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"t authorization. Numeric controls are `searchResults` (1–20, default 5), `imageCount` (1–4, default "},{"id":"p21s6","text":"1), and `videoArtifactTtlMs` (1 hour–7 days, default 7 days; the UI shows 1–168 hours). Lowering vid"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"eo retention shortens and cleans existing artifacts immediately; raising it affects only artifacts c"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"reated afterward. Administrators may provide secret-free composition defaults under plugin config `c"},{"id":"p21s9","text":"apabilities`; live user settings in the `coding-subscription-oauth` settings section override that b"},{"id":"p21s10","text":"ase, and omitting it keeps every switch off."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"`codex-oauth-fast` is advertised only after a **fresh live catalog** lists at least one `priority`-e"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"ligible model. Those requests send `service_tier: priority` plus a routing hint. The UI says **Fast "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"requested** and never guarantees latency or that upstream will honor the request."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Codex search, usage, and images are **opt-in** private `chatgpt.com/backend-api` endpoints. Image ge"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"neration uses the fixed model `gpt-image-2`. Image edit accepts only current-session top-level attac"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"hment ids that this session already owns."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Grok Imagine calls official `https://api.x.ai` with `grok-imagine-image-2.0` and `grok-imagine-video"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"-1.5`. It uses a **separate** DSH credential reference `XAI_API_KEY` — never Grok OAuth and never a "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"process-env fallback. Generated outputs are fetched under MIME / size / time / redirect / DNS contro"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"ls from frozen hosts `imgen.x.ai`, `videogen.x.ai`, and `vidgen.x.ai`, stored privately (256 MiB har"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"d caps for one object and aggregate unique bytes, seven days), and served only on same-origin loopba"},{"id":"p24s6","text":" one object and aggregate unique bytes, seven days), and served only on same-origin loopback routes."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
